Washington, D.C.  Today, U.S. Representative Mike Coffman (R-CO), Chairman of the Subcommittee for Military Personnel for the House Armed Services Committee, applauded the signing into law of the John S. McCain National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA) for Fiscal Year 2019. The NDAA contains significant policy and funding initiatives for the Department of Defense (DoD) and key provisions for Colorado's 6th Congressional District. This is the earliest date both the House and the Senate have passed the NDAA since 1977.
